{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. You’re here because of nausea and vomiting that started this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up vomiting and did it seven times before coming in. I haven’t been able to keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have a history of gastroparesis from your Type 1 diabetes, correct? And a gastric pacer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the pacer was adjusted just a week ago. I was doing so well—no vomiting at all—until today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s frustrating. We’ll need to figure out why this came back. Any fever, pain, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or pain. Just the vomiting. And I haven’t changed my diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good to know. We’ve started IV fluids and anti-nausea meds—Zofran and Reglan. Your blood sugar was high at 256, so we’re watching that closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I couldn’t take my insulin this morning because I was vomiting. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving insulin through the IV to keep it under control. Once you can eat again, we’ll restart your usual glargine at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I was really scared when my oxygen dropped in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was likely from the Ativan—sometimes it can make breathing shallow, especially when you're drowsy from vomiting. Your oxygen is back to normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:08:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. That makes sense. So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray to check for a blockage. It didn’t show any obstruction, which is good. Your pacer is still in place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:09:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s probably my gastroparesis acting up again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely. But we also want to check your esophagus and stomach directly. We’re planning an endoscopy in the next day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like a scope down my throat? Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be sedated, so you won’t feel it. We’ll look for any inflammation or tight spots. Last time, you had a Botox injection to relax the pylorus—that helped, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:12:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it worked great for months. Could I get that again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll see what we find. We may also take a small tissue sample to check for infection or irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:14:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. My blood pressure has been high lately too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been elevated—188 over 86 on admission. Since you’re not on any blood pressure meds, we’re starting you on lisinopril tomorrow if it stays high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:15:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with my kidneys? I’ve had kidney issues before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is normal at 0.8, so your kidneys are doing well. We’ll monitor it. Lisinopril can actually protect your kidneys long-term with diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-01-04 15:17:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good to know. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood cultures came back negative—no infection in the blood. Urine culture was contaminated, so not reliable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no UTI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. No fever or symptoms to suggest it. Your white count is normal too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:32:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my blood sugar? It’s been hard to manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We consulted endocrinology. Once you start eating, your sugars may rise temporarily. We’ll adjust your insulin then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still not hungry. Just the thought of food makes me nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-01-05 08:34:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep giving anti-nausea meds. The endoscopy is scheduled for tomorrow morning. That may help relieve the blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the endoscopy. You did great. We found white patches in your esophagus—signs of a fungal infection called candidiasis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A fungal infection? But I feel fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:01:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common in people with diabetes. We took biopsies, but they didn’t show fungus—still, we’re treating it because the scope findings are clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How do we treat it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "With an antifungal pill—fluconazole. One dose today, then one daily for six days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Did you do the Botox injection too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we injected Botox into your pylorus in five spots. It should help the stomach empty better. That’s often why people with gastroparesis vomit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope it works again. What about the inflammation you mentioned last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsies showed inflammation in your esophagus and stomach—gastritis. We’re starting a stronger acid blocker, pantoprazole, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on something for that before. This is stronger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-01-06 14:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice daily should help reduce irritation and possibly the nausea too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you kept down some apple juice and crackers last night. That’s a big step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was so nervous, but it stayed down. Can I eat more today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:01:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll advance you to a soft diet—things like mashed potatoes, oatmeal. Small, frequent meals are best with gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin? I took my glargine last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we restarted your glargine. Your fasting sugar this morning was 144—excellent. Keep using your humalog as needed with meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. My blood pressure has been better too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-01-07 09:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, on lisinopril, it’s been in the 140s over 80s. Much improved. We’ll keep you on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two full meals and no vomiting. We think you’re ready to go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s wonderful. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adding three: fluconazole for the fungal infection, lisinopril for blood pressure, and pantoprazole twice a day for stomach inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And Zofran for nausea if it comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, take it as needed. But be careful—Zofran can cause constipation. Use senna and docusate if you don’t have a bowel movement in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, see your gastroenterologist in two weeks. They’ll review the biopsy results and check your progress. Also follow up with endocrinology for your diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:05:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I was really worried this would never get better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2198-01-08 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve come a long way. The Botox and treatment for the infection should help. Keep up with small meals and your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. You’re alert, eating well, and your labs are stable. Ready to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I can’t wait. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call us if you start vomiting again, can’t keep fluids down, or have high fevers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll make those follow-up appointments today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and I hope you stay symptom-free."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2198-01-09 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home. We’re glad we could help."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-01-04 14:47:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-01-09 13:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer presented with acute onset of severe vomiting, unable to tolerate oral intake. She had been symptom-free since a prior Botox injection but re-presented after a week of recurrent vomiting. Initial management included IV fluids, antiemetics, and insulin adjustment. An abdominal X-ray ruled out obstruction. An EGD revealed esophageal candidiasis and gastritis; biopsies confirmed active esophagitis and chronic gastritis despite negative fungal staining. She received Botox injection into the pylorus for gastroparesis and was started on fluconazole, pantoprazole, and lisinopril for hypertension. Her symptoms improved, allowing advancement to a soft diet. She was discharged home in stable condition on a revised medication regimen with follow-up planned in gastroenterology and endocrinology.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Candidal esophagitis",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Dehydration"
    ]
  }
}
